# Neo Pulse parameters (docs/specs/neo-pulse.md). The order changes only with a version (machines.md §3.2): songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoPulse
namespace NeoBuzz.Pulse
class NeoPulseMachine
summary Eight-lane Euclidean and probability rhythm generator on note wires: each lane builds a Euclidean step ring (1 to 32 steps, pulses, rotation), a second Euclidean accent ring, per-hit chance, ratchets (1 to 4 repeats with ratchet chance), gate, divider (1x to 4x), note, velocity, accent velocity, MIDI channel and mute. Global clock rate (1/1 to 1/64, straight, dotted or triplet), swing, fill chance, humanize time and velocity, and a repeatable seed (0 = Free). It makes no sound itself: wire it on a note wire to Neo Drums, any synth or another note target. Use it for driving drum kits, polyrhythms, odd-meter grooves, ratcheting hats and polymetric synth lines.

group Clock
Rate        "Rate"              0 9    4    enum 1/1 1/2 1/4 1/8 1/16 1/32 1/64 2_bars 4_bars 8_bars | Base step length at the song tempo
    id rate
    how Sets the base step length at the song tempo, from eight bars down to a sixty-fourth.
    sound Shorter steps run faster rhythms across all eight lanes.
Feel        "Feel"              0 3    0    enum Straight Dotted Triplet Quintuplet | Straight, dotted (1.5x), triplet (2/3x) or quintuplet (4/5x) step feel
    id feel
    how Scales the base step length to straight, dotted (one and a half times as long) triplet (two thirds as long) or quintuplet (four fifths as long).
    sound Dotted steps add a syncopated lilt and triplets create a rolling three-against-two feel.
Swing       "Swing"             0 75   0    int 0 %                             | Delays every odd step by up to 75 % of a step
    id swing
    how Delays every second step of each lane by a share of its step length, from 0 to 75 %.
    sound Higher swing turns straight divisions into a loose, shuffled groove.
HumTime     "Humanize time"     0 20   0    lin 0 20 ms 0                       | Random positive timing offset per hit (0 … 20 ms)
    id humanize_time
    how Delays each hit by a random offset up to this many milliseconds, repeatable for a fixed seed.
    sound Small amounts soften rigid grid timing so percussion feels played by hand.
HumVel      "Humanize velocity" 0 30   0    int 0 %                             | Random velocity variation per hit (0 … 30 %)
    id humanize_velocity
    how Varies each hit velocity randomly up or down by up to this percentage, repeatable for a fixed seed.
    sound Gentle variation stops repeated hits from sounding mechanical.
Fill        "Fill chance"       0 100  0    int 0 %                             | Probability of adding a random hit on empty steps (0 … 100 %)
    id fill_chance
    how Sets the probability that an empty step on any unmuted lane fires an extra random hit.
    sound Low fill values sprinkle occasional ghost notes and high values turn sparse grooves dense.
Seed        "Seed"              0 9999 1    int 0                               | Repeatable random seed (0 = Free, 1 … 9999 = fixed)
    id seed
    how Chooses the seed for chance, fill, ratchet chance and humanize rolls; 0 (Free) varies every run, while 1 to 9999 repeats identically.
    sound A fixed seed locks probabilistic grooves so the same bar plays the same way every time.

group Lane 1
L1Steps     "L1 steps"          1 32   16   int 0                               | Lane 1 step count (1 … 32)
    how Sets how many steps lane 1 cycles through before wrapping around, from 1 to 32.
    sound Lengths that do not divide 16 create polymetric rhythms that shift against the bar.
L1Pulses    "L1 pulses"         0 32   4    int 0                               | Lane 1 Euclidean hit count (0 … steps)
    how Sets how many hits lane 1 distributes evenly across its steps via Bjorklund's algorithm (clamped to steps).
    sound Zero silences the main ring while higher values build denser grooves up to every step.
L1Rot       "L1 rotation"       0 31   0    int 0                               | Lane 1 step rotation (0 … steps − 1)
    how Shifts lane 1's Euclidean hits forward around its step ring by this many steps (clamped to steps minus 1).
    sound Rotating shifts downbeats into off-beats and locks interlocking lanes around each other.
L1Chance    "L1 chance"         0 100  100  int 0 %                             | Lane 1 per-hit probability (0 … 100 %)
    how Sets the probability that each active step on lane 1 fires its note, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Lowering chance drops occasional hits for breathing, evolving percussion.
L1AccPulses "L1 accent pulses"  0 32   0    int 0                               | Lane 1 Euclidean accent count (0 … steps)
    how Sets how many steps in lane 1's second Euclidean accent ring use the accent velocity (clamped to steps).
    sound Accents emphasize selected hits so grooves push and pull dynamically.
L1AccRot    "L1 accent rot"     0 31   0    int 0                               | Lane 1 accent ring rotation (0 … steps − 1)
    how Shifts lane 1's accent ring forward around its steps by this many steps (clamped to steps minus 1).
    sound Moving the accent ring changes which hits pop forward without changing the rhythm itself.
L1Note      "L1 note"           0 127  36   int 0 note                          | Lane 1 MIDI note number (0 … 127)
    how Chooses the MIDI note number lane 1 sends on the note port, from 0 to 127.
    sound Maps the lane to a drum voice in Neo Drums or a pitch on any synth.
L1Vel       "L1 velocity"       1 127  110  int 0                               | Lane 1 normal hit velocity (1 … 127)
    how Sets the MIDI velocity sent for non-accented hits on lane 1, from 1 to 127.
    sound Lower velocities sit quietly as ghost notes and higher values hit harder.
L1AccVel    "L1 accent vel"     1 127  127  int 0                               | Lane 1 accented hit velocity (1 … 127)
    how Sets the MIDI velocity sent when a hit on lane 1 lands on an accented step, from 1 to 127.
    sound Setting this above the base velocity makes accented steps punch through the groove.
L1Gate      "L1 gate"           5 100  50   int 0 %                             | Lane 1 note gate length (5 … 100 % of step)
    how Sets how long each note from lane 1 is held as a share of its step slot, from 5 to 100 %.
    sound Short gates make tight percussive stabs and long gates let synth notes sustain across the step.
L1Ratchet   "L1 ratchet"        1 4    1    int 0                               | Lane 1 repeats inside one step (1 … 4)
    how Subdivides a firing step on lane 1 into 1 to 4 rapid evenly spaced repeats when ratchet chance passes.
    sound Adds crisp snare rolls, hi-hat flurries and rapid melodic trills inside the beat.
L1RatchetCh "L1 ratchet chance" 0 100  100  int 0 %                             | Lane 1 probability of ratcheting a firing hit (0 … 100 %)
    how Sets the probability that a firing hit on lane 1 triggers its ratchet repeats, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Moderate values add occasional surprise rolls without cluttering every hit.
L1Div       "L1 divider"        0 3    0    enum 1x 2x 3x 4x                    | Lane 1 clock divider (1x … 4x slower)
    how Divides the global step rate for lane 1 by 1, 2, 3 or 4 so the lane steps more slowly.
    sound Slower dividers anchor bass notes and slow accents underneath fast percussion lanes.
L1Ch        "L1 channel"        1 16   1    int 0                               | Lane 1 MIDI channel (1 … 16)
    how Selects the MIDI channel lane 1 tags onto its outgoing note messages, from 1 to 16.
    sound Useful when wiring to multi-channel instruments or splitting channels across targets.
L1Mute      "L1 mute"           0 1    0    switch                              | Mutes lane 1 (stops hits and fills)
    how Silences lane 1, immediately releasing any sounding note it owns and blocking both hits and fills.
    sound Lets you drop individual voices in and out of a rhythm without losing their settings.

